      en: "Pharmakina is a leading pharmaceutical company based in Bukavu, South Kivu Province, renowned for its global significance in the production of quinine. Established during the colonial era, the plant has grown into one of Africa's largest producers of anti-malarial treatments, sourcing raw materials from its own Cinchona plantations in the region. The factory plays a crucial role in the local economy, employing hundreds of professionals in the processing of Cinchona bark into active pharmaceutical ingredients. Geographically, Pharmakina benefits from the fertile volcanic soils and cool climate of the Kivu highlands, which provide ideal conditions for the growth of the Cinchona tree. In addition to quinine, the company produces medications for other tropical diseases and makes a vital contribution to healthcare in eastern DRC. Pharmakina is a symbol of industrial permanence in a region often marked by instability and remains a cornerstone of the Congolese pharmaceutical industry.",
