      en: "Sotexki (Société Textile de Kisangani) is a major industrial enterprise in Kisangani, Tshopo Province, forming the backbone of textile production in the northeastern Democratic Republic of the Congo. Established in 1974, the plant specializes in processing locally grown cotton into high-quality textiles, particularly the traditional 'pagne' fabrics. The factory is a key employer in the region and contributes significantly to the value chain of Congolese agriculture. Geographically, the company benefits from its location on the Congo River, which facilitates the transport of goods to other parts of the country. In recent decades, Sotexki has faced significant challenges due to aging machinery and cheap imports but is undergoing modernization processes to increase competitiveness. The plant is a symbol of the industrial ambition of the Mobutu era and remains an indispensable player for the economic revival of Kisangani. Furthermore, its production supports thousands of cotton farmers in the Bas-Uele and Haut-Uele provinces.",
